  "description": "Compute exact scaled dot-product attention utilizing online running maximum and normalizer updates across sequence blocks.\n\nStandard attention materializes O(N^2) memory tensors. Online softmax updates running max and denominator statistics incrementally in fast SRAM cache, avoiding high-bandwidth memory roundtrips.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\mathbf{O} = \\text{Softmax}\\left(\\frac{\\mathbf{Q} \\mathbf{K}^T}{\\sqrt{d}}\\right) \\mathbf{V}\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Compute scaled dot-product attention scores S = (Q K^T) / sqrt(d)\n2. Evaluate numerically stable softmax probabilities along sequence length\n3. Perform context projection by matrix multiplying attention distribution with V\n\n### Returns\nNested 2D list of shape (N, d) representing attention output rounded to 4 decimal places.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Implement FlashAttention with Online Softmax\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNatural language consists of discrete words and symbols arranged in sequential order. To process text with neural networks, we convert words into continuous embedding vectors and model their grammatical and semantic relationships. **Implement FlashAttention with Online Softmax** is a core sequence-processing mechanism used in modern Transformer and LLM architectures.\n\nStandard attention materializes O(N^2) memory tensors. Online softmax updates running max and denominator statistics incrementally in fast SRAM cache, avoiding high-bandwidth memory roundtrips. In this problem, the goal is to: compute exact scaled dot-product attention utilizing online running maximum and normalizer updates across sequence blocks.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{O} = \\text{Softmax}\\left(\\frac{\\mathbf{Q} \\mathbf{K}^T}{\\sqrt{d}}\\right) \\mathbf{V}\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Compute scaled dot-product attention scores S = (Q K^T) / sqrt(d)\n2. **Phase 2**: Evaluate numerically stable softmax probabilities along sequence length\n3. **Phase 3**: Perform context projection by matrix multiplying attention distribution with V\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Self-Attention Mechanics**: Scaled dot-product attention computes all-to-all token interactions dynamically, allowing tokens to gather context from the entire sentence simultaneously.\n* **Position Encodings**: Because self-attention is permutation-invariant, positional encodings (like sinusoidal or Rotary Position Embeddings) inject word order into the representations.\n* **Vocabulary & Subwords**: Algorithms like BPE tokenize text into frequent subwords, allowing models to represent rare words without requiring an infinite vocabulary.",
